prompt_template:
Create one finished art-house editorial poster, expressing a person remembered through shared experiences. Priorities:
{STYLE_FIDELITY_ANCHORS}
Single invented portrait: {SUBJECT}
Memory replacement cells: {MEMORY_FRAGMENTS}
Exact main title: "{MAIN_TEXT}".
Exact small supporting sentence: "{SECONDARY_TEXT}".
Specific narrative and ratio direction: {DESIGN_DIRECTION}
Source exclusions: {SOURCE_CONTENT_TO_AVOID}
Use coarse structured black newspaper halftone on the face, softer grainy faded color on the everyday memories, one pink-black duotone memory cell, warm off-white paper and narrow consistent gutters. The portrait must read as one face from afar, the memories become legible up close. Integrate the title into an intentional blank or merged-cell region. Do not generate a presentation mockup or a sheet of multiple posters. No extra text.
